        },
        {
          "label": "5",
          "html": "Figurą osiowosymetryczną jest trójkąt o kątach wewnętrznych 20°, 20° i 140°."
        }
      ],
      "figures": [],
      "answer": {
        "correct": "FPFPP",
        "solution_html": null,
        "model": {
          "answer": "FPFFP",
          "by": "sonnet",
          "agrees": false,
          "solution_html": "<p>1) Only equilateral triangles have 3 axes, not every triangle → F. 2) A square is a rhombus with 4 axes → P. 3) Only for a square is the diagonal an axis; not for every rectangle → F. 4) A right-angled trapezoid cannot also be isosceles (that would force a rectangle, no longer a proper trapezoid) → F. 5) Triangle 20°,20°,140° is isosceles, so it has an axis of symmetry → P.</p>"
        }
      }
